# Working notes assessing other projects in this space. Kept out of the
# repository: a comparative judgement belongs in a piece of writing that makes
# its argument, dated and attributable, not in a scratch directory that ships
# with a tool. The positioning that IS settled is in docs/DESIGN_RATIONALE.md.
related_tools/

# Corpus. Papers are paywalled or licence-limited and never belong in git.
corpus/
*.pdf
**/*.pdf

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
build/

# Env and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# IDE / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Test and type-check artifacts
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.pyright/
.tox/
.nox/
.hypothesis/

# Extracted text sidecars sit beside their PDF and are regenerated whenever
# the extractor or the normaliser changes. Derived, never source.
corpus/**/*.txt

# Local environment pinning and shells
.python-version
.envrc
.direnv/

# Editor and OS leftovers
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db

# Built documentation
docs/_build/
site/

# Build artifacts
*.egg-info/

# Private design-decision record: kept on disk for a future write-up,
# never part of the published tool. See conversation of 2026-09-01.
docs/DESIGN_RATIONALE.md

# Stray research artifact (GROBID source), never part of the tool.
tl.java

# Adapter/design reasoning: kept on disk, not part of the published tool.
docs/ADAPTERS.md
